:: var.initial [startup]
{=

(set: $testMode to true)

(set: $dice to (random: 1,100))

(set: $log to (a:))

<!--$stuff is a "helper" variable. It is more durable than temporary variables, and it can break out of scope. It is meant to be cleared upon time's advance (displaying "code.timePass"). An example of things that uses $stuff is the $funcCycling macro.-->
(set: $stuff to (dm:))